// check: refuse E_InitPerformsOwnOp
// A handler's state init performs an op that handler itself answers. The
// install's world_push has not run while its inits run — by construction,
// for every install of it — so the singleton dispatch's world_find provably
// returns 0 and the belt beneath it is the only outcome.
//
// SEEN RED at pin c3410610ce41: this compiled to 38467 bytes of WAT and
// trapped at 134. The runtime was already correct and precise — the belt
// named the op, the handler, the extent and the fix — but it said so after
// emitting a module. This is the same verdict at a point where nothing has
// been emitted.
//
// The decidable case: a direct perform lexically inside LHandleWith's own
// `inits`, naming that install's handler. The 1016 sibling guards in the
// wheel's own emit stay belts, because their world lookup is a live runtime
// read that no static extent can discharge.
effect F { g() -> Int }
handler hf with s = g() {
  g() => resume(42),
}
fn main(q) = (g()) ~> hf
